          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most yards, the WORX WG509 TriVac is the leaf vacuum to buy: an 18:1 rated mulch ratio, a two-stage metal impeller, a 1.2-bushel bag and a 3-year warranty in a 9.3-pound corded tool. The Sun Joe SBJ606E is the value pick with the biggest bag, and the Toro UltraPlus pulls hardest in vacuum mode.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Go cordless only if outlets are out of reach or you already own the batteries, and keep leaves dry and debris-free to avoid clogs. If your leaves land mostly on open lawn, a push sweeper or a mulching mower will save you more time than any vacuum.
